# AGENTS Index

[`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) is the **agent index**: identity, skills/agents inventory, and **pointers** to policy SoTs.

It is **not** a policy SoT, Design SoT, module map, UX cookbook, flag encyclopedia, fragile-risk catalog, or milestone tracker.

**Ownership:** [DOC-OWNERSHIP.md](../../.specs/codebase/DOC-OWNERSHIP.md).

## Forbidden in AGENTS.md

- Milestone tags: `\bM\d+\b`
- Changelog voice
- Long CLI fixture example dumps (→ skill `vitals-cli-validation`)
- Normative exit-code **tables** (→ `docs/cli-reference.md`)
- Normative quality-gate / commit / YAGNI prose (→ `quality-gates.mdc`, `commit-policy.mdc`, `coding-guidelines`)
- Design SoT detail, fragile-risk catalogs, UX/flag laundry lists

## Allowed

- `HOTSPOT-*` mentioned only as a pointer to feature-planning naming
- Skills/agents inventory tables
- Short pointers to ARCHITECTURE, DOC-OWNERSHIP, TESTING, ROADMAP/STATE, cli-reference, hooks README, policy rules/skills

## Sync rule

1. Update AGENTS **only** when identity or skills/agents inventory changed — policy text lives in SoTs.
2. Self-check: *Does this sentence need a milestone number to make sense?* If yes → ROADMAP/STATE/feature specs.

Editorial lint: [living-sot-doc.mjs](../hooks/lib/living-sot-doc.mjs) `lintAgentsDoc`.
